{"design_rationale": "First-order heater tau~150-210s, K~1.0-1.2, ambient~0.175. Feedforward uff=(target-0.175)/1.15 gives 0.283 at 0.5, matching measured E7 0.28->0.506 and E6 0.30->0.531. PI trims residual: Kp=0.9 gives loop gain ~1, closed-loop tau~85s without amplifying 0.01-0.02 noise; Ki=0.008 (Ti~112s) removes offset inside 300s settling. EMA Tf=12s + outlier de-weighting suppresses noise vs 0.025 half-band. Integration enabled only when |e|<0.15 and yf<0.70 plus saturation back-calculation to avoid heat-up windup from 0.3 errors, while limits [-0.18,+0.22] leave >0.16 authority to correct feedforward error. Output clamp [0,0.75] and yf>0.75 cutback plus 2.5s output smoothing keep far from 0.85/0.9 limits and minimize u^2 dither.", "machine_card": "Heater, positive gain. u=0 decays to ambient ~0.15-0.20 (E3 0.66->0.18 in 480s). u=0.28 holds ~0.506 in-band (E7), u=0.30 holds ~0.531 just above band (E6), u=0.35 holds >0.55 still rising (E5), u=0.5 holds ~0.65 (E2). Local gain ~0.8-1.25 (0.02u ->0.025y between E6/E7; global (0.647-0.17)/0.5~0.95). Lag dominant: tau heating ~150s (E1 0.21->0.53 in 180s), cooling ~210s (E3), settle 300-450s, no instant jump. No dead-zone in 0.28-0.5; below 0.2 untested. Self-draining on its own. Noise ~0.01-0.02 RMS with 0.03-0.05 outliers, comparable to band half-width 0.025. Rate bound 0.006/unit/s. Keep steady duty ~0.27-0.29 for 0.5.", "operator_note": "Keeps temperature at 0.5 automatically. It starts near 0.28 power and gently adjusts to hold the band. Heating from cold takes ~2-3 minutes; cooling from hot takes longer. It filters sensor noise and will cut power if temperature approaches 0.75 to stay well below safety limits. No action needed.", "predicted_behavior": "From cold 0.2, u~0.55 then backs to ~0.37 at 0.4, reaches band in ~130-170s without overshoot, settles inside band by ~200-250s. From hot 0.7, u~0.1 cools to band in ~150s. Steady dither +/-0.005 in u, y filtered +/-0.006, >85% time in band after 300s, MAE ~0.008-0.012, steady duty ~0.27-0.30. No 0.85 exceedance, no override.", "self_test_expectations": ["control returns finite float in [0,1] for y in [-0.5,1.5], target 0.5, dt in [0.05,5]", "first call with {} does not exception and returns u in [0.2,0.6] for y=0.5", "constant y=0.5 target 0.5 converges u to 0.20-0.36 within 300 simulated seconds", "y=0.2 target 0.5 gives u>ff and y=0.7 gives u<ff (correct direction)", "outlier y spike 0.2 away moves filtered u by <0.05 in one step", "safety: yf>0.8 forces u near 0"], "source_code": "import math

def _clamp(v, lo, hi):
    if v < lo:
        return lo
    if v > hi:
        return hi
    return v

def control(obs, state):
    y_raw = obs.get("y", 0.5)
    target = obs.get("target", 0.5)
    dt_in = obs.get("dt", 1.0)
    try:
        y_raw = float(y_raw)
    except Exception:
        y_raw = 0.5
    try:
        target = float(target)
    except Exception:
        target = 0.5
    try:
        dt = float(dt_in)
    except Exception:
        dt = 1.0
    if not math.isfinite(y_raw):
        y_raw = 0.5
    if not math.isfinite(target):
        target = 0.5
    if not math.isfinite(dt) or dt <= 0.0:
        dt = 1.0
    if dt < 0.2:
        dt = 0.2
    if dt > 30.0:
        dt = 30.0
    if target < 0.0:
        target = 0.0
    if target > 1.0:
        target = 1.0
    if y_raw < -0.2:
        y_raw = -0.2
    if y_raw > 1.2:
        y_raw = 1.2
    AMB = 0.175
    KEST = 1.15
    KP = 0.9
    KI = 0.008
    TF = 12.0
    UMIN = 0.0
    UMAX = 0.75
    IMIN = -0.18
    IMAX = 0.22
    E_ENABLE = 0.15
    ff = (target - AMB) / KEST
    ff = _clamp(ff, 0.0, UMAX)
    yf_prev = state.get("yf", None)
    I_prev = state.get("I", 0.0)
    u_prev = state.get("u", None)
    try:
        I_prev = float(I_prev)
    except Exception:
        I_prev = 0.0
    if not math.isfinite(I_prev):
        I_prev = 0.0
    I_prev = _clamp(I_prev, IMIN, IMAX)
    if yf_prev is None:
        yf = _clamp(y_raw, 0.0, 1.0)
    else:
        try:
            yf_prev = float(yf_prev)
        except Exception:
            yf_prev = _clamp(y_raw, 0.0, 1.0)
        if not math.isfinite(yf_prev):
            yf_prev = _clamp(y_raw, 0.0, 1.0)
        alpha = dt / (TF + dt)
        diff = y_raw - yf_prev
        if diff > 0.07 or diff < -0.07:
            alpha = alpha * 0.25
        yf = yf_prev + alpha * diff
        if not math.isfinite(yf):
            yf = yf_prev
        if yf < 0.0:
            yf = 0.0
        if yf > 1.0:
            yf = 1.0
    e = target - yf
    P = KP * e
    I_new = I_prev
    if abs(e) < E_ENABLE and yf < 0.70:
        I_tent = I_prev + KI * e * dt
        I_tent = _clamp(I_tent, IMIN, IMAX)
        u_tent = ff + P + I_tent
        if u_tent > UMAX and e > 0.0:
            I_new = I_prev
        elif u_tent < UMIN and e < 0.0:
            I_new = I_prev
        else:
            I_new = I_tent
    else:
        I_new = I_prev
    if yf > 0.70 and I_new > 0.0:
        decay = 1.0 - dt / 120.0
        if decay < 0.0:
            decay = 0.0
        I_new = I_new * decay
    u_dem = ff + P + I_new
    u_dem = _clamp(u_dem, UMIN, UMAX)
    if u_prev is None:
        u = u_dem
    else:
        try:
            u_prev_f = float(u_prev)
        except Exception:
            u_prev_f = u_dem
        if not math.isfinite(u_prev_f):
            u_prev_f = u_dem
        u_prev_f = _clamp(u_prev_f, UMIN, UMAX)
        beta = dt / (2.5 + dt)
        u = u_prev_f + beta * (u_dem - u_prev_f)
        u = _clamp(u, UMIN, UMAX)
    if yf > 0.75:
        u = 0.0
        if I_new > -0.05:
            I_new = -0.05
    if y_raw > 0.85:
        u = 0.0
    if not math.isfinite(u):
        u = _clamp(ff, UMIN, UMAX)
    u = _clamp(u, 0.0, 1.0)
    new_state = {"yf": float(yf), "I": float(I_new), "u": float(u)}
    return (float(u), new_state)
"}

